                            <comment id="17083787" author="slukyanov" created="Wed, 15 Apr 2020 04:20:34 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;I&apos;m now working on a draft of the approach #2 - treat REPLICATED as PARTITIONED.&lt;br/&gt;
It seems to be doable relatively cheap. The limitation with this approach is that it requires the primary partitions of REPLICATED and PARTITIONED caches to be collocated, i.e. the REPLICATED cache needs to have the same affinity key and affinity function.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
